ling a module containing  the immune activation immune cell typing  tumor profiling and the immune oncology  drug targeting that module  and then we selected rois based on  tissue microenvironment versus the tumor  so the the regions of interest that we  were selected were based on the entire  tma core so one tumor core uh  contained two regions of interest so the  the trimmer mask was stained with the  pancetta keratin antibody and you can  see this on the left hand side  uh the mask below shows the white which  was the areas which were selected  the tumor microenvironment was selected  based on the cd45 a pan leukocyte  antibody  and again you can see below this the  white area denotes the marked area that  was  selected for white area  this slide just gives you an overview of  the type of  cores that we were seeing so the tissue  microwave was  generated and back in the day  when we first started the clinical trial  and so you can see they're selected for  a tumor only um however you can see that  there's  areas that have high um infiltrates that  you can see the bottom  right hand side here and we have areas  which have a lower  lower immune infiltrator but they're  still present in sort of top left here  so the actual dsp analysis so as i said  originally the br9601 recruited 374  patients  we made tissue microarrays from 321  patients  but the actual dsp expression analysis  was performed on 256 patients  these were equally distributed in that  129 of those patients received epirusion  and 120 received cmf only  the first sort of analysis we did was we  compared  our dsp analysis with a traditional in  historic chemistry ihc so on the  left-hand side you can see a plot that  gives us  um k-67 staining with ihd and that's  along the bottom  x-axis and then you can see the dsp uh  tumor t67 staining  on the the y-axis and here we see a  correlation of 0.66  on the right-hand side we have a  correlation looking at her2 expression  so again on the x-axis we can see ihd  her2 scores versus the tumor her2 scores  from the dsp and here we have a  correlation  of 0.81 so within this analysis we can  see that there are significant  correlation between the dsp  and ihd analyses  we also looked at predictive clustering  by regions of interest morphology  and then you can see here that the tumor  expression  cluster together compared to the tme  cluster in a different  way alt denoting that the expression  between the tumor and the tremor mic  environment can be very different  we then went on to look at the  differential protein expression based on  distant relapse free survival  so this volcano plot gives you single  protein expressions  in orange we have protein expression the  tumor compartment and in blue we have  a protein expression based on the tumor  micro environment  and we looked at a false discovery rate  of 10  so within this analysis we had 14  proteins that were statistically  significant associated with  distant relapse tree survival and these  included ffe  alpha e7h3 and cd8  within the tumor microenvironment  compartment we had 13 proteins that were  significantly associated with distant  relapse free survival  and these included fibronectin f b alpha  again  and b spell  we then went on to look at the  correlation between the probes  and we were able to show that there's a  large cluster of co-expressed immune  proteins there's a strong correlation  between  tumor t cell markers uh with macrophages  in the t  in the tumor microenvironment there was  also negative correlation of strong  markers  such as fibronectin and epcam in the  tumor microenvironment  with some of the immune proteins such as  b73 e7 h3  and ctla4  we derived a t-cell score using the  average expression of cd3  and cd4 and cd8 and we weren't able to  say that there was  a wealth of patients that had  t cell invasion you can see this denoted  in the red  we had patients where we see t styles  exploded so there were there was t-cells  present but they were did not invade  into the  into the tumor and then we have an area  where there's t-cell cold  as it is expected to see in breast  cancer  we also went on to show that proteins  that were most associated with t  cell explosion so in this blue  compartment were fibrin actin and b7h3  and here's the figures that show this so  high tumor t  scale scores were really occurred in the  presence of high  uh b7 or h3 or fibrinectin in the titan  tumor microenvironment  indicating this would be an interesting  analysis to do some further analyses  with  furthermore we then went on to look at  some of the other pathway important  pathways and cell types expressions in  the treatment micro environment  as this volcano plot gives just hazard  ratios again with the distance from  electricity survival  and the blue denotes the tumor  microenvironment proteins or pathways  and then and they sort of marine color  we give the the  proteins or the pathways that are in the  tumor compartment  within the tumor microenvironment we saw  the high expression of myeloid  suppression  mhc2 apoptosis and macrophages were  associated with improved dystrophy  survival  however when we look at the tumor  compartment we can see that  fibroblasts and checkpoint inhibitors  are associated with a poorer  survival um when we look at the tumor  compartment  if we look at some of the single  biomarkers as a productive  predictive or prognostic biomarkers so  these um  these grass should count the mars of  survival with their distant relaxed free  survival  so the top graph gives us the prognostic  uh role of the outcome  in the tumor micro environment um across  the bottom we have  the time in years and then we have the  percentage of a distant relapse free  survival  uh blue denotes the patients that have  low expression and then residents  patients with high expression  and we can see that epcom with patients  with a high high epcam  in the tumor microenvironment do worse  compared to the 