l types  identified numerous pathways and self  ties that were  prognostic in this setting and we have  potential predictive biomarkers  including webcam and hltr  and these are the people that actually  helped us perform the study  thank you dr spears for a very nice talk  i have some question for you too can you  please  comment why it is important to look at  the role of the tumor microenvironment  in the antracycline response  it's important to look at anthrocyclines  in the tumor microenvironment and that  we know that some patients respond to  anthracycline and some patients don't  as i said during my presentation the use  of anthracycline can be  significantly toxic to these patients  and so we really need to identify  a biomarker response so identifying  those patients who  will respond and those patients that  don't uh we've looked at the tumor  microbiota the tumor  now for a number of years and so i think  it's important to now look across the  tumor microenvironment  as we learn more and more about the  the area  thank you what novel information  did the geomics technology show that  other technology  couldn't achieve  i think the dsp allowed us to look at  across numerous  proteins uh within one single slide  and so we're able to identify new and  potential uh predictive biomarkers of  response  thank you very much how could this work  be used in the pre-clinical setting  some of the work that we could be doing  the pre-clinical setting includes  looking at somebody's organized and how  the microenvironment plays a role in  treatment response  and i think this is where we could use  potentially the dsp technology  thank you how could the results present  here  have an impact in the clinical setting  i think the results here need to be  validated but i think with the dsp has  the potential to identify new biomarkers  that could be both proteomic and rna and  they could be  essentially then moved into the clinical  aspect  the next steps for this study would be  to validate any new findings and publish  it  we also have another other studies that  we want to look at and look at the micro  environment and the role it plays  in in breast cancer pathology  thank you again dr spears for your  presentation and discussion

